# vss reads this file ITSELF since 2026-09-09, not only through systemd.
# Copy it to ~/.config/vss/vss.env (chmod 600) and every route finds the
# values: an interactive `vss briefing` or `vss xbrl` reads the same file
# the units do. THE ENVIRONMENT STILL WINS -- a variable set in the shell
# overrides the file, so `VSS_SEC_CONTACT=x vss xbrl ...` does what it
# says. See vss/env.py.
#
# Environment for the vss units. Copy to ~/.config/vss/vss.env and fill in.
# THE REAL FILE IS NEVER COMMITTED: the topic is the only secret ntfy has.
#
# Shape is plain KEY=value with no quoting and no export, so the same file
# is readable by systemd's EnvironmentFile= and by a shell:
#     set -a; . ~/.config/vss/vss.env; set +a

# E92: where the nightly run POSTs its NEEDS OWNER pointer. A bare topic
# name is completed to https://ntfy.sh/<topic>; a full URL is used as given,
# so a self-hosted server needs no second variable. Unset is SILENCE, not an
# error. OUTBOUND ONLY -- nothing here ever reads from the topic.
NTFY_TOPIC=

# THE DEAD MAN'S SWITCH, leg 4: the OUTSIDE observer (owner, 2026-09-01).
#
# A healthchecks.io ping URL. `vss.service` GETs it as ExecStartPost, i.e.
# only when the nightly run SUCCEEDED, and healthchecks.io alarms when the
# ping does not arrive within its grace period. That is the only alarm a
# powered-off VPS can still raise, because raising it needs nothing from the
# VPS. Legs 1-3 all run here and all go silent with the machine.
#
# ONE OPAQUE UUID, ONE GET, NO BODY. No ticker, no price, no report, no
# hostname ever leaves the machine -- the far end learns that something it
# knows only as a UUID is alive, and nothing else.
#
# Unset is SILENCE, not an error (E92). Suggested settings at the far end:
# period 1 day, grace 6 hours -- the run is 22:30 daily with Persistent=true.
HEALTHCHECK_URL=

# `vss watch`'s own, older topic URL. Deliberately separate from the above:
# a refresh pointer is not a disclosure alert, and either may be set alone.
#VSS_NTFY_URL=

# The contact address data.sec.gov asks callers to declare (vss xbrl).
#VSS_SEC_CONTACT=

# SEC EDGAR's access policy requires a contact in the User-Agent: your name
# and an e-mail, e.g. "Jane Doe jane@example.com". Needed by `vss xbrl`,
# `vss watch` (SEC arm) and the report reader. Nothing is invented if unset.
VSS_SEC_CONTACT=

# OPTIONAL -- the report reader (`vss earnings`, `vss watch --read`). An
# OpenRouter API key; the model only EXTRACTS figures with their source
# sentence, and every judgement is made by rules.py. Unset: the reader is off.
VSS_OPENROUTER_KEY=
# Any OpenRouter model id; default deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash (vss/extract.py).
VSS_OPENROUTER_MODEL=

# OPTIONAL -- where `vss watch` posts "a filing is out". Kept separate from
# NTFY_TOPIC by design; a full URL, e.g. https://ntfy.sh/<your-topic>.
VSS_NTFY_URL=
